174	// ===========================================================================
175	// Real install/remove — per-source adapters over SSH.
176	//
177	// Approach: the worker resolves a DIRECT download URL from the source's API, then
178	// SSHes into the game VM and has the VM itself `curl` the file into the game's
179	// plugin/mod directory (deterministic filename, so uninstall is a plain rm — no
180	// per-install state to track). Sources that need auth or per-repo handling
181	// (GitHub release zips, Nexus, CurseForge key, Codefling paid) soft-fail with a
182	// clear "install manually from <url>" note rather than faking success.
183	//
184	// Supported today: modrinth + spigotmc (Minecraft), umod (Rust), thunderstore
185	// (Valheim) — which fully covers those three games' catalogs — plus github
186	// TShock plugins (Terraria), which need a restart-and-verify step the others
187	// don't: see the Terraria section below `removeModReal`. `steam_workshop`
188	// mods use a completely different mechanism — see the big Steam Workshop
189	// section near the end of this file — and never go through planTarget/
190	// resolveUrl/modDirShell below at all.
191	// ===========================================================================
