1147	/**
1148	 * Empyrion — NOT pure config-write, and NOT a growing list: the official
1149	 * wiki's `dedicated.yaml` reference has exactly one relevant key,
1150	 * `CustomScenario`, and it takes a SINGLE local folder name, not a Workshop
1151	 * id or a list. So unlike every other family here, Empyrion can only have
1152	 * ONE active Workshop scenario at a time — attempting a second install while
1153	 * one is already active is refused rather than silently replacing it.
1154	 *
1155	 * Mechanism: `steamcmd workshop_download_item` (Valve's own tool, run inside
1156	 * the customer's own container — bitr/empyrion-server documents a generic
1157	 * `STEAMCMD=` passthrough env var for exactly this kind of one-off command)
1158	 * fetches the scenario into the container's own workshop content cache; we
1159	 * then copy it into `Content/Scenarios/` under a fixed name and point
1160	 * `dedicated.yaml`'s `CustomScenario` at it.
1161	 *
1162	 * CONFIDENCE NOTE: the exact internal path layout under this image's mounted
1163	 * volume (`/opt/empyrion` on the host, `/home/user/Steam` in the container)
1164	 * is discovered at run time via `find` rather than hardcoded, because no
1165	 * official source documents it precisely — if `dedicated.yaml` or
1166	 * `Content/Scenarios` can't be located, this fails honestly instead of
1167	 * guessing a path and silently writing nothing (or writing to the wrong
1168	 * place).
1169	 */
1170	const EMPYRION_APPID = WORKSHOP_APPID.empyrion;
