1811	// --- Satisfactory — ficsit.app (the Satisfactory Mod Repository) -----------
1812	//
1813	// New mod source for this pass. ficsit.app is the game's community mod
1814	// repository (the one Satisfactory Mod Manager itself uses); its GraphQL API
1815	// (api.ficsit.app/v2/query) and file downloads (api.ficsit.app/v1/version/
1816	// <id>/<target>/download → storage.ficsit.app) are public and keyless —
1817	// checked live 2026-09-30. Every version lists its build targets; only
1818	// `LinuxServer` builds are installable on Nxeon's Linux server
1819	// (wolveix/satisfactory-server). Mods load through SML (Satisfactory Mod
1820	// Loader, itself a mod — mod_reference "SML"), which every mod declares as a
1821	// dependency, so the ordinary dependency walk installs it too. Each mod goes
1822	// in FactoryGame/Mods/<mod_reference>/ (the .smod archive is a zip of that
1823	// folder's contents), which is where SML/SMM look for it. The server's own
1824	// install root is /config/gamefiles in the container = host
1825	// /opt/satisfactory/gamefiles (wolveix run.sh: `+force_install_dir
1826	// /config/gamefiles`).
